//! The `rule-visibility-items` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS)
//! [shorthand](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Cascade/Shorthand_properties)
//! property defines whether rule segments are painted in both row and column gaps adjacent to empty
//! areas.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - all: Rules should be painted in all gap segments, regardless of whether adjacent areas contain
//! an item.
//! - around: A rule should be painted in a gap segment if at least one of the two adjacent areas is
//! occupied by an item.
//! - between: A rule should be painted in a gap segment only if both adjacent areas are occupied by
//! items.
//! - normal: With grid containers, behaves the same as `all`. In multicol layout, behaves the same
//! as `between`. This is the default.
//!
//! Grammar: <'column-rule-visibility-items'>
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-gaps-1/#propdef-rule-visibility-items
//!
//! Author guide:
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/rule-visibility-items
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

